  "body": "Though the spec says [user agents should not honor the lazy loading attribute when scripting is disabled](https://whatpr.org/html/3752/urls-and-fetching.html#attr-loading-lazy-state), but as far as I can see there is no description when it's done.\r\n\r\nI have [an interesting edge case](https://github.com/hiikezoe/web-platform-tests/commit/a66aac1b16dd03a759c26a6681641dcc2bf6b0a3), that is that an image element which is in the state waiting for load due to 'lazy\" is moved into an iframe that script is disabled there.   I was guessing the image in question is not loaded on Chrome because, as per the spec text, there seems no chance to check it after the image became the state of 'will-lazy-load-image-steps', but actually Chrome does.\r\n\r\n@domfarolino, @annevk, @emilio ",
